Self-hosted web fonts.

Currently empty: the site loads DM Sans and JetBrains Mono from Google Fonts,
behind a full system-font fallback stack, so it degrades cleanly when the CDN
is blocked or offline.

To self-host instead (avoids the third-party request, improves privacy, and
removes a point of failure):

  1. Download the woff2 files into this directory
  2. Replace the <link> tags in portfolio/index.html with @font-face rules
     in portfolio/css/main.css
  3. Use font-display: swap so text renders before the font arrives

Note: web fonts are used on the WEBSITE only. The email deliverables use no
web fonts at all — email clients strip @font-face.
